On 22.06.2013 18:40, georgiosmierscheid@gmail.com wrote:
> I'm currently playing a wizard with an amulet of reflection and a cloak of
> magical resistance and I'm wondering how they are different. Is reflection
> the same as magical resistance with added reflection? Or are there more
> properties which differ?

Well, reflection reflects rays/beams/breaths, and magic resistance provides
resistance against certain magic effects. - Why do you think they have in
some way commonalities?

Typically you want to get both. Magic resistance (MR) protects for example
against polymorph traps, against [level] teleport and energy drain traps.
MR also protects against magical armour disintegration from powerful high
level spell-casters, and from the touch of death attack. Reflection helps
against breath attacks from dragons (including disintegration), against
offensive wands like fire, cold, death, magic missile. Reflection protects
also from the gaze attack of floating eyes, and (as long as you are not
invisible) also from Medusa's stoning gaze. There are certainly a couple
more applications, but you get the point.

